## Worksheet

**F1 – Core loop**: `gameState` single object; `mulberry32(seed)` stored as `gameState.rng`, used in generateMap/fireEvent/triggerAshstorm/trade; `endTurn()` calls production→colonists→ashstorm→event→trade in fixed order. Score 2.

**F2 – Map**: 8x8 loop in `generateMap()`, terrain from `gameState.rng()`; `buildBuilding()` checks `building.terrain.includes(tile.terrain)`; but adjacency bonus checks `adj.type === 'water'` against building-type field, and no building type is named `'water'`, so it never fires. Score 1.

**F3 – Economy**: chain geothermal(power)→condenser(water)→greenhouse(food) via `resolveProduction()`; caps enforced/overflow logged in `updateResources()`. (`updateStorageCaps()` is dead code, minor.) Score 2.

**F4 – Population**: colonists have skill/fatigue/morale/job; `skillBonus` in `resolveProduction()` reads `c.skill`, but fatigue is never read by production code. Score 1.

**F5 – Needs**: consumption in `updateColonists()`, shortage drops morale -15, fatigue/morale recovery drift exists; but morale is never read in `resolveProduction()` — output formula ignores it. Score 1.

**F6 – Research**: 8 nodes in `RESEARCH_TREE`, prereqs enforced in `researchAvailable()`, costs deducted in `doResearch()`; but `mining`, `morale-boost`, `trade-hub` unlock effects are never read anywhere. Score 1.

**F7 – Events**: 10 events in `EVENTS`, all with 2 differing-effect choices; `recentEvents` Set gives cooldown; but selection is uniform `EVENTS[floor(rng()*len)]`, no weighting. Score 1.

**F8 – Trade**: `updateTradeprices()` reads `gameState.globalSupply`; `tradeInventory` capped and decremented; `tradeResource()` buy/sell both mutate resources/scrip/supply. Score 2.

**F9 – Hazard**: `checkAshstorm`/`triggerAshstorm` fire periodically, severity scales with turn, reduced by `ashfilter` research and watchtowers, `repairBuilding` costs parts; but `resolveProduction()` never checks `b.health`/`b.damaged`, so damaged buildings produce at full rate. Score 1.

**F10 – Save/load**: `serializeGame()` → JSON text in textarea; `deserializeGame()` parses with try/catch and `alert()`s on bad input. Score 2.

**F11 – End conditions**: `checkEndConditions()` has reachable win (turn≥60,pop≥12,food/water≥30) and lose (pop≤0); `calculateScore()` uses turn/pop/research/scrip; `renderEndScreen()` shown. Score 2.

**F12 – UI**: `switchTab()` wired to buttons; log entries show `entry.turn`; keyboard shortcuts in `keydown` listener; `@media` responsive CSS; but `tooltipBonus` field is defined per-building and never rendered anywhere. Score 1.

**F13 – Dev panel**: `runTests()` has 15 real invariant assertions (caps, prereqs, terrain, pop==colonists); `runBenchmark()` runs 200 headless `endTurn()` calls and prints `gameStateHash()`. Score 2.

**G1**: `doResearch` sets `researchDone`; `resolveProduction()` reads `researchDone.has('smelting-adv'/'hydroponics'/'industry')` to multiply output every turn. Score 4.

**G2**: shortage → `c.morale -=15` in `updateColonists()`; but morale never feeds `resolveProduction()` directly — only indirect effect is colonist removal at morale≤0 shrinking `b.workers` matches. Score 2.

**G3**: `triggerAshstorm` sets `b.health/b.damaged`; `repairBuilding` restores health and costs parts; but `resolveProduction()` never reads health/damaged, so output loss link is absent. Score 1.

**G4**: `tradeResource` mutates `globalSupply`; `updateTradeprices` recomputes prices from `globalSupply` each caravan visit (not per-transaction). Score 3.

**G5**: `dust-found`/`refugee`/`colonist-sick` choice effects write distinct mutations (`resources.parts`, `population`, `colonists.push`, `morale`/`fatigue`) via `resolveEvent()`. Score 4.

